    <main class="about-page">
        <h1>So, who else climbs here?</h1>
        <p>You start recognizing people at the gym after a while. Same shoes, same chalk bag, always working on that one
            climb. But you might not know much else about them.</p>
        <p>Nice to “Climb” You NYC is a place to share a little about yourself and see who else climbs at your gym. It’s
            not about your grade. Tell us what you like climbing, what holds you avoid, or what happened when you said
            “one more try.” Again.</p>

        <h2>Which cat are you?</h2>
        <p>Take the quiz to get one of these four climbing cats. It’s just for fun. You might be a different one next
            week.</p>
        {# these introductions grow with the text, unlike the fixed-size cards on the wall #}
    <section class="about-type">
            <img src="/images/cat_beta.png" alt="Beta detective cat">
            <h2>The Beta Detective</h2>
            <p>You’ve done the moves in your head several times before touching the wall. Sometimes the plan works.
                Sometimes the hold is much worse than it looked from down there.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="about-type">
            <img src="/images/cat_stubborn.png" alt="One-more-try cat">
            <h2>The One-More-Try</h2>
            <p>Your friends are putting their shoes away. You’re still saying “wait, I think I know what I did wrong.”
                You said that three tries ago, but this time you mean it.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="about-type">
            <img src="/images/cat_wander.png" alt="Wanderer cat">
            <h2>The Wanderer</h2>
            <p>You came in to work on one climb and somehow tried everything else. Something across the room looked fun.
                Then something else did.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="about-type">
            <img src="/images/cat_mat.png" alt="Mat cheerleader cats">
            <h2>The Mat Cheerleader</h2>
            <p>You’ve been sitting on the mat for twenty minutes, but you’ve cheered for six people and made a friend. A
                pretty good session, honestly.</p>
        </section>

        <h2>Leave a card. Have a look around.</h2>
        <p>Click the holds on the home page to fill out your card. Add your cat type, climbing favorites, home gym, and
            a short story. You can preview it before deciding to share.</p>
        <p>Then look through the Community wall, or filter by your gym. Maybe someone else is stuck on the same move.
            Maybe you’ve already climbed next to them without saying anything.</p>
        <p>The cards are anonymous, so you get to wonder a little. “Wait, could this be the person I keep accidentally
            making eye contact with?” Possibly. Or you both just hate slopers. Either way, now you have something to
            talk about.</p>
        <p class="note">Cards are public, so leave out identifying details. This class-project version keeps cards only
            until the server restarts.</p>
        <a class="button" href="/">Make a card ↗</a>
